--- THIRD-PARTY NOTICES ---

ComfyUI-MoCapAnything-V2 (Windows / ComfyUI port) changes to the notice above:

- The RMBG-1.4 network definition (preprocess/briarmbg.py, (c) BRIA AI) has been
  REMOVED from this version. preprocess/briarmbg.py is now only an alias for
  preprocess/mit_matting.py. No RMBG-1.4 code or weights are used or downloaded.

- Models downloaded at runtime from their own repositories under their own
  licences (not redistributed in this package):
    MoCapAnything V2 weights  kehong/MoCapAnythingV2-weights   MIT
    BiRefNet                  ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet              MIT
    InSPyReNet (fallback)     transparent-background package   MIT
    DINOv2-large              facebook/dinov2-large            Apache-2.0
    SAM2.1 hiera base-plus    facebook/sam2.1-hiera-base-plus  Apache-2.0
    T5-base                   google-t5/t5-base                Apache-2.0

- vendor/roma: roma 1.5.4, BSD-3-Clause, (c) NAVER Corp. (see vendor/roma/LICENSE)

- No Truebones Zoo motion data is included in this package. The released
  MoCapAnything V2 weights were trained on data that includes Truebones Zoo
  (https://truebones.gumroad.com/l/skZMC); see the original repository for the
  status of the training-data licence.
